The Attack Scenario
Vulnerability: WebSecurityGroup allowed SSH (Port 22) from 0.0.0.0/0.

Compromise: Attacker (44.252.71.199) connected via SSH and created a backdoor user chaos-user.

Impact: The website was defaced (image replaced).

Detection: CloudTrail logs and local aureport logs revealed the unauthorized access.

Remediation: The rogue user was killed/deleted, SSH was hardened, the Security Group was restricted, and the IAM user was deleted.

Recovery: The defaced website image was restored from backup.

Security Design (Remediation)
Least Privilege: SSH restricted to specific IP (102.254.46.3/32).

Hardening: PasswordAuthentication disabled in sshd_config.

Audit: CloudTrail logs analyzed via Athena for forensic evidence.

Cleanup: Unauthorized IAM user chaos deleted.

Recovery: Defaced image restored using sudo mv Coffee-and-Pastries.backup Coffee-and-Pastries.jpg.
